    "description": "Maxell XLII 90\nHigh Bias Type II Blank Audio Cassettes\nLot of 3 Sealed Tapes\nThe Maxell XLII is an iconic Type II high-bias cassette formulation renowned for its low noise, wide dynamic range, and consistent high-frequency response. Featuring the classic packaging with the legendary Steve Steigman \"Blown Away\" chair visual, these tapes were designed specifically to capture the clarity of digital audio and CD sources. Manufactured in Japan, Maxell XLII cassettes remain highly sought after by vintage audio enthusiasts and recording hobbyists.\nHigh Bias IEC Type II formulation with 70s equalization\n90 minutes total recording time (2 x 45 minutes) / 135 meters (443 feet)\nLot includes 3 individually factory-sealed blank audio cassette tapes in original cellophane\nMade in Japan as indicated on rear packaging\nCondition:\nAll three cassette tapes are brand new and factory sealed in original manufacturer shrink wrap. The clear plastic wrap is fully intact on each tape with no tears, holes, or unsealed seams. Jewel cases and internal j-cards appear pristine beneath the wrap.",
